INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### HTTP/HTTPS & Networking: Deep Dive into TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake

**Role Focus**: Backend Developer | **Difficulty**: Hard | **Language/Stack**: Python, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, Go

#### Architectural Overview
In Backend Developer environments, TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake within HTTP/HTTPS & Networking plays a pivotal role in system reliability and efficiency. Understanding the underlying mechanics of TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake ensures that implementations scale predictably under production workloads.

#### Core Principles & Mechanism
1. **Core Mechanism**: TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake enforces deterministic execution and guarantees correctness across distributed or modular components.
2. **State & Lifecycle**: Proper management of TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake mitigates resource contention, memory leaks, and race conditions.
3. **Performance Implications**: Using TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake appropriately optimizes computational complexity, typically achieving O(1) or O(log N) operations.

#### Production Best Practices
- Always validate boundary constraints and edge cases when working with TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake.
- Implement thorough unit and integration testing to catch regression errors early.
- Monitor metrics and telemetry around TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake to prevent degradation under high traffic.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "HTTP/HTTPS & Networking", "subtopic": "TCP/IP 3-Way Handshake", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "languages": ["Python", "Java", "JavaScript", "TypeScript", "Go"], "source": "InterviewMind-AI-Curated-Dataset-v1"}'::jsonb)
