INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### OOP Design Patterns: Deep Dive into Factory Pattern

**Role Focus**: Java Developer | **Difficulty**: Easy | **Language/Stack**: Java

#### Architectural Overview
In Java Developer environments, Factory Pattern within OOP Design Patterns plays a pivotal role in system reliability and efficiency. Understanding the underlying mechanics of Factory Pattern ensures that implementations scale predictably under production workloads.

#### Core Principles & Mechanism
1. **Core Mechanism**: Factory Pattern enforces deterministic execution and guarantees correctness across distributed or modular components.
2. **State & Lifecycle**: Proper management of Factory Pattern mitigates resource contention, memory leaks, and race conditions.
3. **Performance Implications**: Using Factory Pattern appropriately optimizes computational complexity, typically achieving O(1) or O(log N) operations.

#### Production Best Practices
- Always validate boundary constraints and edge cases when working with Factory Pattern.
- Implement thorough unit and integration testing to catch regression errors early.
- Monitor metrics and telemetry around Factory Pattern to prevent degradation under high traffic.', '{"role": "Java Developer", "role_id": "java_developer", "topic": "OOP Design Patterns", "subtopic": "Factory Pattern", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Easy", "languages": ["Java"], "source": "InterviewMind-AI-Curated-Dataset-v1"}'::jsonb)
